   "text": "During the 1860s to early 1880s Warrandyte quartz prospecting was extensive but only very limited success; most reefs were worked down to the water table and abandoned. Crushing was poor: in 1860 a 4-head battery and Chilian mill, pronounced defective in 1861; in 1875 only one crusher, water-driven and useless when the river flooded.",
