   "text": "The Queenstown Government Battery (75 Smiths Gully Road) was opened soon after the First World War and used intermittently. Its weatherboard battery house burned in a 1962 bushfire and the machinery was removed. Surviving remains are timber mortar blocks of a 5-head battery, concrete mounting blocks and floor, a concrete weir in the creek, and a cyanide works (small dumps of battery sand, a galvanised iron vat and a poison tank).",
