   "text": "Lewis Grant, who introduced a water-powered stamping battery in the Yarra about 1868, formed the Yarra Tunnelling Co. in 1869 to work a claim just upstream of The Island. The tunnel ran 70 feet beneath the river with shafts to both banks. Water seepage was manageable and pumping kept the workings dry. Grant sold to David Mitchell in 1874; the mine reopened in 1884 with good returns and closed again in 1888.",
