   "text": "In early June 1851 Melbourne city solicitor Francis Stephen and Dr Miller (who had worked California mines) went to the Plenty Ranges with a spade and returned on a Thursday with about 1.5 oz of pure gold found on the surface. Stephen gave charts of the spot to others and handed the gold to Commissioner of Crown Lands James Simpson. A fall down a precipice stopped further search.",
