   "id": 800,
   "text": "In May 1906 the Caledonia Star Company mine (formerly Redleap) had crushed 203 tons for 674 oz from a reef 2 inches to 2 feet wide, and the Ormond reef (sunk 350 ft by the first owners) was taken up by a company with machinery. Old miner Withers was sinking a 150 ft shaft alone, at 30 ft.",
