   "text": "In June 1906 the Arthur's Creek Gold-mining Company reported a payable sheet of gold cut in the south level at 200 ft and driven on for 60 ft. 610 tons crushed for 400 oz worth 1923 pounds, all from Gardner's claim. The north level was at 210 ft and a 135 ft level was being extended.",
