   "id": 840,
   "text": "A 1938 Argus feature says Henry Hurst, living on the Diamond Creek station leased from Cornelius Haley (at present Hurstbridge), crushed a projecting rock with a bullock wagon wheel and found gold-studded quartz. He kept the site secret to buy the station, was shot by bushranger Burke a few weeks later and died without telling his brother Frederick. Hundreds of searches have failed.",
