   "id": 1035,
   "text": "Jutson judged the quartz reefs shown by Moon and Whitelaw outside the Warrandyte area (including towards Kangaroo Ground and Croydon) to be thin, irregular and in country where the geological structure does not favour fractures, so he saw little hope of a new goldfield beyond Warrandyte.",
