   "id": 1044,
   "text": "In March 1926 the Age said gold mining was still commercial near Panton Hill; specimens from the Try Again mine, between Hurstbridge and Panton Hill, were displayed in Melbourne and its recent average crushing went 73 oz 5 dwt to the ton.",
