   "place": "Jumping Creek, Andersons Creek (Fourth Hill) and Stoney Creek, Warrandyte State Park",
   "summary": "A guide to the three creeks in Warrandyte State Park where prospecting is allowed. At Jumping Creek the presenter stands on the Jumping Creek Road bridge and says only the upstream side is open; access is a steep bank with no safe parking. At Andersons Creek he parks at the Fourth Hill car park on Gold Memorial Road and shows the orange markers about 10-20 m beyond each State Forest sign; only the creek bed between them is open, and the fire track must not be dug. At Stoney Creek he describes the Yarra end, reached from Warrandyte-Research Road and The Boulevard, with the road bridge as the upper limit; the gold there carries more black sand than Andersons Creek and suits beginners. No gold is recovered on camera; the video is about where and how, and he says the creeks are for beginners, not big returns.",
