   "place": "Stoney Creek, Warrandyte State Park",
   "summary": "Crevicing on Stoney Creek. About eight buckets from a pond-side crack give nothing; a pan from the bottom of the crack using a yabby pump and other crevices give only specks, which the presenter puts down to fast water. The useful find is an abandoned tailings pile of clay-bound rock left by another digger: a pan from it shows gold because the clay was never broken up, so the advice is to process the clay. The total for a few hours is about 0.16 (unit not spoken, probably grams) plus a bucket to process at home. He suspects someone used a high banker on the creek and states that high bankers are not allowed in the three park creeks, only pans and cradles.",
