   "summary": "This video is outside the study area. The video names no place; a news report puts the find in bushland at Ballarat, about 100 km west of Warrandyte, in May 2024. It is included as a comparison between metal detecting on a nugget field and panning creek gold at Warrandyte. The presenter detects with a Minelab GPX 6000 on a wet day, finds ten small nuggets within about an inch of the surface in red clay and pipe clay (under a gram in total), then digs a faint deep target about two pinpointers deep beside an old miner's hole and recovers an egg-sized nugget of 868 g (about 27.9 troy oz; the title's 1 kg is rounded up). Warrandyte creek finds in the other three videos are fractions of a gram, and detecting off the creek beds is not allowed in Warrandyte State Park.",
